Doctor: hi I can understand the issue it is basically the facial muscle spasm that you have in the classical pattern it involves larger areas of the face and not smaller area or single muscle the cause for it can be mild compression more of irritation than compression over the nerve which runs into the facial muscles the site of compression can be near its origin secondary to pressure from a neighboring blood vessel the less common cause can be viral involvement of the nerve in the ear for that you should be investigated with the torch panel viral screening test depending on results we can plan further management a short therapeutic course of steroids may help if it persists for a long time then botox injection into the muscle to inactivate it will help',
