Doctor: hello welcome to icliniq com twitches are seen in als amyotrophic lateral sclerosis however they usually start in the hands and are accompanied by the thinking of muscles or atrophy of muscles a much more common cause of twitches is anxiety leading to hyperventilation leading to decreased calcium level in the blood in your case the most likely cause of twitches is anxiety however since I cannot conclusively rule out the possibility of als I suggest you do nerve conduction studies which can diagnose als please feel free to followup with the nerve conduction study report and we can discuss in detail',
